IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc22-juries.l4 -- sections 626 to 644 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: juries; challenging the panel; empanelling the jury; excusing, challenging and discharging jurors). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.
-- The sheriff and "an officer of the court" are not constructors of the core's Party, and no regulative rule here names them: they are facts (BOOLEAN) in the decision functions.

§ `Section 626 -- Qualification of jurors`

-- src:12919 | 626 (1) A person who is qualified as a juror according to, and summoned as a juror in accordance with, the laws of a province is qualified to serve as a juror in criminal proceedings in that province.
@ref s 626(1) (src:12919-12919)
GIVEN `the person is qualified as a juror according to the laws of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is summoned as a juror in accordance with the laws of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are criminal proceedings in that province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 626(1) the person is qualified to serve as a juror in criminal proceedings in the province` MEANS
    IF `the person is qualified as a juror according to the laws of the province` AND `the person is summoned as a juror in accordance with the laws of the province` AND `the proceedings are criminal proceedings in that province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is qualified and summoned is for the laws of the province

-- src:12921 | (2) Notwithstanding any law of a province referred to in subsection (1), no person may be disqualified, exempted or excused from serving as a juror in criminal proceedings on the grounds of his or her sex.
@ref s 626(2) (src:12921-12921)
GIVEN `the ground is the person’s sex` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 626(2) the person may be disqualified, exempted or excused from serving as a juror on that ground` MEANS
    IF `the ground is the person’s sex`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person may be disqualified, exempted or excused from serving as a juror in criminal proceedings on the grounds of his or her sex" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the grounds of his or her sex"

-- src:12923 | 626.1 The judge before whom an accused is tried may be either the judge who presided over matters pertaining to the selection of a jury before the commencement of a trial or another judge of the same court.
@ref s 626.1 (src:12923-12923)
GIVEN `the judge presided over matters pertaining to the selection of a jury before the commencement of the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is another judge of the same court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 626.1 the judge before whom the accused is tried may be this judge` MEANS
    IF `the judge presided over matters pertaining to the selection of a jury before the commencement of the trial` OR `the judge is another judge of the same court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be either the judge who presided over matters pertaining to the selection of a jury before the commencement of a trial or another judge of the same court"

-- src:12925 | 627 The judge may permit a juror with a physical disability who is otherwise qualified to serve as a juror to have technical, personal, interpretative or other support services.
@ref s 627 (src:12925-12925)
GIVEN `the person is the judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the juror has a physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the juror is otherwise qualified to serve as a juror` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 627 the judge may permit the juror to have technical, personal, interpretative or other support services` MEANS
    IF `the person is the judge` AND `the juror has a physical disability` AND `the juror is otherwise qualified to serve as a juror`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The judge may permit a juror with a physical disability who is otherwise qualified to serve as a juror"

-- src:12928 | 628 [Repealed, R.S., 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 129]
