§ `Section 629 -- Challenging the jury panel`

-- src:12930 | 629 (1) The accused or the prosecutor may challenge the jury panel only on the ground of partiality, fraud or wilful misconduct on the part of the sheriff or other officer by whom the panel was returned.
@ref s 629(1) (src:12930-12930)
DECLARE `s 629(1) the ground of challenge to the jury panel` IS ONE OF
    `s 629(1) partiality on the part of the sheriff or other officer by whom the panel was returned`
    `s 629(1) fraud on the part of the sheriff or other officer by whom the panel was returned`
    `s 629(1) wilful misconduct on the part of the sheriff or other officer by whom the panel was returned`
    `s 629(1) some other ground`

-- src:12930 | 629 (1) The accused or the prosecutor may challenge the jury panel only on the ground of partiality, fraud or wilful misconduct on the part of the sheriff or other officer by whom the panel was returned.
@ref s 629(1) (src:12930-12930)
GIVEN `the challenger is the accused or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 629(1) the ground of challenge to the jury panel`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 629(1) the accused or the prosecutor may challenge the jury panel` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the challenger is the accused or the prosecutor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The accused or the prosecutor may challenge the jury panel"
        IF ground EQUALS `s 629(1) some other ground` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may challenge the jury panel only on the ground of partiality, fraud or wilful misconduct" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12932 | (2) A challenge under subsection (1) shall be in writing and shall state that the person who returned the panel was partial or fraudulent or that he wilfully misconducted himself, as the case may be.
@ref s 629(2) (src:12932-12932)
GIVEN `the challenge is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the challenge states that the person who returned the panel was partial or fraudulent or that they wilfully misconducted themself, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 629(2) the challenge is in the form subsection (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the challenge is in writing` AND `the challenge states that the person who returned the panel was partial or fraudulent or that they wilfully misconducted themself, as the case may be`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be in writing and shall state that the person who returned the panel was partial or fraudulent or that he wilfully misconducted himself" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12934 | (3) A challenge under this section may be in Form 40.
@ref s 629(3) (src:12934-12934)
GIVEN `the challenge is made under section 629` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 629(3) the challenge may be in Form 40` MEANS
    IF `the challenge is made under section 629`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A challenge under this section may be in Form 40"

-- src:12936 | 630 Where a challenge is made under section 629, the judge shall determine whether the alleged ground of challenge is true or not, and where he is satisfied that the alleged ground of challenge is true, he shall direct a new panel to be returned.
@ref s 630 (src:12936-12936)
GIVEN `a challenge is made under section 629` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the alleged ground of challenge is true` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 630 the judge must determine whether the ground is true and, if satisfied that it is, direct a new panel to be returned` MEANS
    IF `a challenge is made under section 629`
    THEN (IF `the judge is satisfied that the alleged ground of challenge is true` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section says what follows where the judge is satisfied and is silent on what follows where the judge is not
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a challenge is made under section 629, the judge shall determine whether the alleged ground of challenge is true or not" [M-a] [F:duty]

§ `Section 631 -- Empanelling jury`

-- src:12940 | 631 (1) The name of each juror on a panel of jurors that has been returned, his number on the panel and his address shall be written on a separate card, and all the cards shall, as far as possible, be of equal size.
@ref s 631(1) (src:12940-12940)
GIVEN `a panel of jurors has been returned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 631(1) the name, number and address of each juror must be written on a separate card, the cards being as far as possible of equal size` MEANS
    IF `a panel of jurors has been returned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The name of each juror on a panel of jurors that has been returned"

-- src:12942 | (2) The sheriff or other officer who returns the panel shall deliver the cards referred to in subsection (1) to the clerk of the court who shall cause them to be placed together in a box to be provided for the purpose and to be thoroughly shaken together.
@ref s 631(2) (src:12942-12942)
GIVEN `the cards referred to in subsection (1) have been written` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 631(2) the sheriff or other officer who returns the panel must deliver the cards to the clerk of the court, who must have them placed in a box and shaken` MEANS
    IF `the cards referred to in subsection (1) have been written`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the cards referred to in subsection (1)"

-- src:12944 | (2.1) If the judge considers it advisable in the interests of justice to have one or two alternate jurors, the judge shall so order before the clerk of the court draws out the cards under subsection (3) or (3.1).
@ref s 631(2.1) (src:12944-12944)
GIVEN `the judge considers it advisable in the interests of justice to have one or two alternate jurors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of alternate jurors` IS A NUMBER
      `the clerk of the court has drawn out the cards under subsection (3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 631(2.1) the judge must order alternate jurors before the clerk of the court draws out the cards` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge considers it advisable in the interests of justice to have one or two alternate jurors` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge considers it advisable in the interests of justice to have one or two alternate jurors, the judge shall so order" [M-a] [F:duty]
        IF (NOT (`the number of alternate jurors` EQUALS 1)) AND (NOT (`the number of alternate jurors` EQUALS 2)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "one or two alternate jurors"
        IF `the clerk of the court has drawn out the cards under subsection (3) or (3.1)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the judge shall so order before the clerk of the court draws out the cards under subsection (3) or (3.1)" (the time has passed) [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12944 | (2.1) If the judge considers it advisable in the interests of justice to have one or two alternate jurors, the judge shall so order before the clerk of the court draws out the cards under subsection (3) or (3.1).
@ref s 631(2.1) (src:12944-12944)
DECLARE `s 631(2.1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 631(2.1) order that one or two alternate jurors be sworn`

@ref s 631(2.1) (src:12944-12944)
GIVEN `the time at which the clerk of the court draws out the cards` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 631(2.1) action`
`s 631(2.1) the judge must order alternate jurors before the draw` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 631(2.1) order that one or two alternate jurors be sworn`
    WITHIN `the time at which the clerk of the court draws out the cards`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the judge considered alternate jurors advisable but did not so order before the clerk of the court drew out the cards"

-- src:12946 | (2.2) If the judge considers it advisable in the interests of justice, he or she may order that 13 or 14 jurors, instead of 12, be sworn in accordance with this Part before the clerk of the court draws out the cards under subsection (3) or (3.1).
