        IF `the number of persons who have answered is, in the opinion of the judge, sufficient to provide a full jury and any alternate jurors ordered by the judge, after allowing for orders to excuse, challenges and directions to stand by` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the number of persons who have answered is, in the opinion of the judge, sufficient to provide a full jury" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

