        IF NOT `the number of persons who answer under subsection (3) or (3.1) is not sufficient to provide a full jury and the number of alternate jurors ordered by the judge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the number of persons who answer under subsection (3) or (3.1) is not sufficient to provide a full jury and the number of alternate jurors ordered by the judge, the clerk of the court shall proceed" [M-a] [F:duty]
