      reason IS A `s 632 the reason`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 632 the judge may order that the juror be excused from jury service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order is made before the commencement of the trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before the commencement of a trial" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a) of 2026-11-05) [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF reason EQUALS `s 632 some other reason` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for reasons of (a) personal interest in the matter to be tried; (b) relationship with the judge ...; or (c) personal hardship or any other reasonable cause"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

