§ `Section 635 -- Order of challenges`

-- src:12970 | 635 (1) The accused shall be called on before the prosecutor is called on to declare whether the accused challenges the first juror for cause, and after that the prosecutor and the accused shall be called on alternately, in respect of each of the remaining jurors, to first make such a declaration.
@ref s 635(1) (src:12970-12970)
DECLARE `s 635(1) the party` IS ONE OF
    `s 635(1) the accused`
    `s 635(1) the prosecutor`

-- src:12970 | 635 (1) The accused shall be called on before the prosecutor is called on to declare whether the accused challenges the first juror for cause, and after that the prosecutor and the accused shall be called on alternately, in respect of each of the remaining jurors, to first make such a declaration.
@ref s 635(1) (src:12970-12970)
GIVEN `the place of the juror in the order in which the jurors are called (1 for the first juror)` IS A NUMBER
      party IS A `s 635(1) the party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 635(1) the party is called on first to declare whether it challenges the juror for cause` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the place of the juror in the order in which the jurors are called (1 for the first juror)` LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no juror before the first
        IF `the place of the juror in the order in which the jurors are called (1 for the first juror)` EQUALS 1 THEN (IF party EQUALS `s 635(1) the accused` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The accused shall be called on before the prosecutor is called on to declare whether the accused challenges the first juror for cause" [M-a]
        IF (`the place of the juror in the order in which the jurors are called (1 for the first juror)` MODULO 2) EQUALS 0 THEN (IF party EQUALS `s 635(1) the prosecutor` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after that the prosecutor and the accused shall be called on alternately, in respect of each of the remaining jurors, to first make such a declaration" [M-a] [F:duty]
        OTHERWISE (IF party EQUALS `s 635(1) the accused` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the prosecutor and the accused shall be called on alternately" [M-a] [F:duty]

DECLARE `s 635(2) the order the accused follow` IS ONE OF
    `s 635(2) the order in which their names appear in the indictment`
    `s 635(2) another order agreed on by them`
    `s 635(2) some other order`

-- src:12972 | (2) Subsection (1) applies where two or more accused are to be tried together, but all of the accused shall exercise the challenges of the defence in turn, in the order in which their names appear in the indictment or in any other order agreed on by them,
-- src:12973 | (a) in respect of the first juror, before the prosecutor; and
-- src:12974 | (b) in respect of each of the remaining jurors, either before or after the prosecutor, in accordance with subsection (1).
@ref s 635(2) (src:12972-12974)
GIVEN `two or more accused are to be tried together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order the accused follow` IS A `s 635(2) the order the accused follow`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 635(2) all of the accused exercise the challenges of the defence in turn in a permitted order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `two or more accused are to be tried together` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) applies where two or more accused are to be tried together, but all of the accused shall exercise the challenges of the defence in turn"
        IF `the order the accused follow` EQUALS `s 635(2) some other order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the order in which their names appear in the indictment or in any other order agreed on by them" [M-a] [F:duty]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12973 | (a) in respect of the first juror, before the prosecutor; and
-- src:12974 | (b) in respect of each of the remaining jurors, either before or after the prosecutor, in accordance with subsection (1).
@ref s 635(2)(a) and (b) (src:12973-12974)
GIVEN `the place of the juror in the order in which the jurors are called (1 for the first juror)` IS A NUMBER
      `the accused exercise the challenges of the defence before the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 635(2)(a) the defence declares as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the place of the juror in the order in which the jurors are called (1 for the first juror)` EQUALS 1
    THEN (IF `the accused exercise the challenges of the defence before the prosecutor` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in respect of the first juror, before the prosecutor" [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- (b): "in respect of each of the remaining jurors, either before or after the prosecutor, in accordance with subsection (1)"

-- src:12975 | 636 and 637 [Repealed, 1992, c. 41, s. 2]
@ref s 636 and 637 (repealed) (src:12975-12975)
`s 636 and 637 what the text shows` MEANS "[Repealed, 1992, c. 41, s. 2]"

§ `Section 638 -- Challenge for cause`

-- src:12977 | 638 (1) A prosecutor or an accused is entitled to any number of challenges on the ground that
-- src:12978 | (a) the name of a juror does not appear on the panel, but no misnomer or misdescription is a ground of challenge where it appears to the court that the description given on the panel sufficiently designates the person referred to;
-- src:12979 | (b) a juror is not impartial;
-- src:12980 | (c) a juror has been convicted of an offence for which they were sentenced to a term of imprisonment of two years or more and for which no pardon or record suspension is in effect;
-- src:12981 | (d) a juror is not a Canadian citizen;
-- src:12982 | (e) a juror, even with the aid of technical, personal, interpretative or other support services provided to the juror under section 627, is physically unable to perform properly the duties of a juror; or
-- src:12983 | (f) a juror does not speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or the official language of Canada in which the accused can best give testimony or both official languages of Canada, where the accused is required by reason of an order under section 530 to be tried before a judge and jury who speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or the official language of Canada in which the accused can best give testimony or who speak both official languages of Canada, as the case may be.
@ref s 638(1) (src:12977-12983)
DECLARE `s 638(1) the ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 638(1)(a) the name of the juror does not appear on the panel`
    `s 638(1)(b) the juror is not impartial`
    `s 638(1)(c) the juror has been convicted of an offence for which they were sentenced to a term of imprisonment of two years or more and for which no pardon or record suspension is in effect`
    `s 638(1)(d) the juror is not a Canadian citizen`
    `s 638(1)(e) the juror, even with the aid of support services provided under section 627, is physically unable to perform properly the duties of a juror`
    `s 638(1)(f) the juror does not speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or in which the accused can best give testimony, or both official languages, as an order under section 530 requires`
    `s 638(1) some other ground`

-- src:12977 | 638 (1) A prosecutor or an accused is entitled to any number of challenges on the ground that
-- src:12978 | (a) the name of a juror does not appear on the panel, but no misnomer or misdescription is a ground of challenge where it appears to the court that the description given on the panel sufficiently designates the person referred to;
-- src:12979 | (b) a juror is not impartial;
-- src:12980 | (c) a juror has been convicted of an offence for which they were sentenced to a term of imprisonment of two years or more and for which no pardon or record suspension is in effect;
-- src:12981 | (d) a juror is not a Canadian citizen;
-- src:12982 | (e) a juror, even with the aid of technical, personal, interpretative or other support services provided to the juror under section 627, is physically unable to perform properly the duties of a juror; or
-- src:12983 | (f) a juror does not speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or the official language of Canada in which the accused can best give testimony or both official languages of Canada, where the accused is required by reason of an order under section 530 to be tried before a judge and jury who speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or the official language of Canada in which the accused can best give testimony or who speak both official languages of Canada, as the case may be.
@ref s 638(1) (src:12977-12983)
GIVEN `the challenger is a prosecutor or an accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 638(1) the ground`
      `the facts bring the juror within the ground` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description given on the panel sufficiently designates the person referred to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order under section 530 requires the accused to be tried before a judge and jury who speak the official language or both official languages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 638(1) the prosecutor or the accused is entitled to challenge the juror for cause on the ground` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the challenger is a prosecutor or an accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A prosecutor or an accused is entitled to any number of challenges"
        IF ground EQUALS `s 638(1) some other ground` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): this function speaks to the grounds of (1); subsection (2) says what follows for any other ground
        IF NOT `the facts bring the juror within the ground` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to any number of challenges on the ground that" (the ground is not made out) [F:entitled] [M-a]
        IF ground EQUALS `s 638(1)(a) the name of the juror does not appear on the panel` AND `the description given on the panel sufficiently designates the person referred to` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no misnomer or misdescription is a ground of challenge where it appears to the court that the description given on the panel sufficiently designates the person referred to" [M-a]
        IF ground EQUALS `s 638(1)(f) the juror does not speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or in which the accused can best give testimony, or both official languages, as an order under section 530 requires` AND (NOT `an order under section 530 requires the accused to be tried before a judge and jury who speak the official language or both official languages`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused is required by reason of an order under section 530 to be tried before a judge and jury who speak the official language of Canada" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12985 | (2) No challenge for cause shall be allowed on a ground not mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 638(2) (src:12985-12985)
GIVEN ground IS A `s 638(1) the ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 638(2) a challenge for cause is allowed on the ground` MEANS
    IF ground EQUALS `s 638(1) some other ground`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No challenge for cause shall be allowed on a ground not mentioned in subsection (1)" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on a ground not mentioned in subsection (1)"

