-- src:12995 | 640 (1) If a challenge is made on a ground mentioned in section 638, the judge shall determine whether the alleged ground is true or not and, if the judge is satisfied that it is true, the juror shall not be sworn.
@ref s 640(1) (src:12995-12995)
GIVEN `a challenge is made on a ground mentioned in section 638` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the alleged ground is true` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 640(1) the judge must determine whether the ground is true and, if satisfied that it is, the juror shall not be sworn` MEANS
    IF `a challenge is made on a ground mentioned in section 638`
    THEN (IF `the judge is satisfied that the alleged ground is true` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says the juror shall not be sworn if the ground is true and is silent otherwise
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a challenge is made on a ground mentioned in section 638, the judge shall determine whether the alleged ground is true or not" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12997 | (2) On the application of the accused or prosecutor or on the judge’s own motion, the judge may order the exclusion of all jurors, sworn and unsworn, from the court room until it is determined whether the ground of challenge is true if the judge is of the opinion that the order is necessary to preserve the impartiality of the jurors.
@ref s 640(2) (src:12997-12997)
GIVEN `the application is made by the accused or the prosecutor, or the judge acts on their own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the order is necessary to preserve the impartiality of the jurors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 640(2) the judge may order the exclusion of all jurors from the court room until it is determined whether the ground of challenge is true` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made by the accused or the prosecutor, or the judge acts on their own motion` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the application of the accused or prosecutor or on the judge’s own motion"
        IF NOT `the judge is of the opinion that the order is necessary to preserve the impartiality of the jurors` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge is of the opinion that the order is necessary to preserve the impartiality of the jurors" [F:may-if]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12999 | 641 (1) If a full jury and any alternate jurors have not been sworn and no cards remain to be drawn, the persons who have been directed to stand by shall be called again in the order in which their cards were drawn and shall be sworn, unless excused by the judge or challenged by the accused or the prosecutor.
@ref s 641(1) (src:12999-12999)
GIVEN `a full jury and any alternate jurors have not been sworn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no cards remain to be drawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is excused by the judge or challenged by the accused or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(1) the person who was directed to stand by must be called again and sworn` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a full jury and any alternate jurors have not been sworn` AND `no cards remain to be drawn`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a full jury and any alternate jurors have not been sworn and no cards remain to be drawn, the persons who have been directed to stand by shall be called again" [M-a] [F:duty]
        IF `the person is excused by the judge or challenged by the accused or the prosecutor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be sworn, unless excused by the judge or challenged by the accused or the prosecutor" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13001 | (2) If, before a person is sworn as a juror under subsection (1), other persons in the panel become available, the prosecutor may require the cards of those persons to be put into and drawn from the box in accordance with section 631, and those persons shall be challenged, directed to stand by, excused or sworn, as the case may be, before the persons who were originally directed to stand by are called again.
