        IF NOT `the person is an alternate juror` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Alternate jurors shall attend at the commencement of the presentation of the evidence on the merits and ... shall replace any absent juror"
        IF `the place of the alternate juror in the order in which their cards were drawn under subsection 631(3)` AT MOST `the number of jurors absent when the evidence on the merits begins` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if there is not a full jury present, shall replace any absent juror, in the order in which their cards were drawn" (no absent juror remains for this alternate) [M-a] [F:duty]

