GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 643(3) the failure to comply affects the validity of a proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the section whose directions were not complied with` EQUALS 643 OR `the section whose directions were not complied with` EQUALS 631 OR `the section whose directions were not complied with` EQUALS 635 OR `the section whose directions were not complied with` EQUALS 641
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with the directions of this section or section 631, 635 or 641 does not affect the validity of a proceeding" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this section or section 631, 635 or 641"

§ `Section 644 -- Discharge of juror`

-- src:13021 | 644 (1) Where in the course of a trial the judge is satisfied that a juror should not, by reason of illness or other reasonable cause, continue to act, the judge may discharge the juror.
@ref s 644(1) (src:13021-13021)
GIVEN `in the course of a trial the judge is satisfied that a juror should not, by reason of illness or other reasonable cause, continue to act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 644(1) the judge may discharge the juror` MEANS
    IF `in the course of a trial the judge is satisfied that a juror should not, by reason of illness or other reasonable cause, continue to act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in the course of a trial the judge is satisfied that a juror should not, by reason of illness or other reasonable cause, continue to act, the judge may discharge the juror" [F:may-where] [M-a]

-- src:13023 | (1.1) A judge may select another juror to take the place of a juror who by reason of illness or other reasonable cause cannot continue to act, if the jury has not yet begun to hear evidence, either by drawing a name from a panel of persons who were summoned to act as jurors and who are available at the court at the time of replacing the juror or by using the procedure referred to in section 642.
@ref s 644(1.1) (src:13023-13023)
DECLARE `s 644(1.1) the way the replacement juror is selected` IS ONE OF
    `s 644(1.1) by drawing a name from a panel of persons who were summoned to act as jurors and who are available at the court at the time of replacing the juror`
    `s 644(1.1) by using the procedure referred to in section 642`
    `s 644(1.1) some other way`

-- src:13023 | (1.1) A judge may select another juror to take the place of a juror who by reason of illness or other reasonable cause cannot continue to act, if the jury has not yet begun to hear evidence, either by drawing a name from a panel of persons who were summoned to act as jurors and who are available at the court at the time of replacing the juror or by using the procedure referred to in section 642.
@ref s 644(1.1) (src:13023-13023)
GIVEN `a juror by reason of illness or other reasonable cause cannot continue to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jury has not yet begun to hear evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `s 644(1.1) the way the replacement juror is selected`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 644(1.1) the judge may select another juror to take the place of the juror` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a juror by reason of illness or other reasonable cause cannot continue to act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a juror who by reason of illness or other reasonable cause cannot continue to act"
        IF NOT `the jury has not yet begun to hear evidence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the jury has not yet begun to hear evidence" [F:may-if]
        IF way EQUALS `s 644(1.1) some other way` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "either by drawing a name from a panel ... or by using the procedure referred to in section 642"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13025 | (2) Where in the course of a trial a member of the jury dies or is discharged pursuant to subsection (1), the jury shall, unless the judge otherwise directs and if the number of jurors is not reduced below ten, be deemed to remain properly constituted for all purposes of the trial and the trial shall proceed and a verdict may be given accordingly.
@ref s 644(2) (src:13025-13025)
GIVEN `a member of the jury dies or is discharged pursuant to subsection (1) in the course of a trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of jurors remaining` IS A NUMBER
      `the judge otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 644(2) the jury is deemed to remain properly constituted for all purposes of the trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a member of the jury dies or is discharged pursuant to subsection (1) in the course of a trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in the course of a trial a member of the jury dies or is discharged pursuant to subsection (1), the jury shall" [M-a]
        IF `the judge otherwise directs` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge otherwise directs" [F:unless] [M-a]
        IF `the number of jurors remaining` LESS THAN 10 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the number of jurors is not reduced below ten" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13027 | (3) If in the course of a trial the number of jurors is reduced below 10, the judge may, with the consent of the parties, discharge the jurors, continue the trial without a jury and render a verdict.
@ref s 644(3) (src:13027-13027)
GIVEN `in the course of a trial the number of jurors is reduced below 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 644(3) the judge may discharge the jurors, continue the trial without a jury and render a verdict` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `in the course of a trial the number of jurors is reduced below 10` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in the course of a trial the number of jurors is reduced below 10, the judge may" [F:may-if]
        IF NOT `the parties consent` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the consent of the parties"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
